      <h2>Self-check</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <p>Not graded. Tap an answer to see if you got it, and read why.</p>
      <Quiz id="quiz-rb" questions={quiz} />

      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li>A red-black tree is a BST where every node is red or black.</li>
          <li>Root is black. NIL leaves are black. No two reds in a row. Same number of blacks on every path down.</li>
          <li>New nodes are red. The only possible problem is red-red (or a red root in an empty tree).</li>
          <li><b>Red uncle → recolor</b> (and check higher). <b>Black uncle → rotate</b> (line: 1, triangle: 2) and swap colors.</li>
          <li>The root always ends up black.</li>
          <li>In code, a rotation must also fix every <code>parent</code> link.</li>
          <li>Red-black trees are a little less balanced than AVL trees but rotate less often. Java's <code>TreeMap</code> uses one.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <p><b>Next unit:</b> Graphs.</p>

